  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1045 AM CDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\n500mb charts show we will stay in a northwesterly flow through the \nweekend, and combine that with a brief northward jaunt of the \nstationary front, we can expect to see more rain showers Sunday into \nMonday morning. This should be the last of it, with the final push \nof cold air following behind it and giving us crisp, fall-like \ntemperatures. At least initially. Highs for the work week will \ninitially be in the 70s, but slowly warm back into the low 80s as \nthe week wears on. The morning lows are where the chilly air \nreally shines, as temperatures will dip into the 40s and 50s \nacross the area through mid-week next week. Probably a bit too \nearly to break out the fall wardrobe, but maybe incorporate some \ncardigans or flannels if you feel so inclined next week.",
